Hmm.  I see crowning as equally beneficial for everyone--not
incredibly so, but it's not infrequent that I still need some
resistances at that point.  The prayer timeout thing is kind of a joke
since after the very early game you only need to pray the one time for
holy water; I try to save another prayer for emergencies but I don't
think I've ever actually used or wanted it post-crowning.

+Finger of Death, meh.  I think I've cast that spell maybe a couple
times ever.  The only time it'd really be helpful is against Rodney
(the first time) or the high priest, after that with the amulet I'm
wanting my PW more for teleports and other stuff.  In practice, I just
use /death since I almost never run out of charges of that anyway, or
cone of cold (which doesn't miss) or similar if I'm going to cast..

Unlocking longsword skill for lawfuls is vaguely useful I guess,
probably moreso than the +FoD to me.


